@startuml architecture_overview
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #E8F4FF

title Challenge -- System Architecture

component "VideoProcessor" as VP
component "VideoClipper" as VC
component "EventNotifier" as EN
component "CPUWatcher" as CW

database "Shared Memory\n/video_shm" as SHM #FFF3D0
queue "UNIX Socket\n/tmp/event_sock.sock" as SOCK #D8E8FF

VP -down-> SHM : WriteFrame()\n(sem_ mutex +\nframe_ready_sem_ signal)
SHM -down-> VC : ReadFrame()\n(waits on\nframe_ready_sem_)

EN -down-> SOCK : send() on 'e'\n(termios raw mode,\ninstant, no Enter)
SOCK -down-> VC : recv()\n(dedicated thread)

CW .right.> VC : reads /proc/PID/*\n(CPU % + memory,\nno IPC)

note right of VC
  frame_cache_: rolling 9s buffer (deque)

  pending_clips_: one entry per active
  trigger, each with its own 9s snapshot
  + independent 6s timer -- supports
  multiple concurrent triggers

  shared_ptr on pixel data: overlapping
  snapshots reference the same buffer,
  no duplication
end note

note bottom
  All 4 programs shut down cleanly on Ctrl+C:
  every blocking wait (semaphores, select(),
  termios, sleep_until) uses a short timeout
  so the stop signal is checked regularly.
end note

@enduml